Troubleshooting Tips
Issue: Metasploit payload doesn't execute

Solution: Check file permissions with ls -l, ensure executable bit is set
Verify listener is running before executing payload
Issue: Python script can't find psutil module

Solution: Install with pip3 install --user psutil
Verify installation with python3 -c "import psutil"
Issue: Permission denied when running containment

Solution: Some actions require sudo privileges
Run script with: sudo python3 containment_automation.py
Issue: No incidents detected after exploitation

Solution: Ensure payload is still running with ps aux | grep payload
Check if listener captured connection in Metasploit
Conclusion
This lab provided hands-on experience with the complete incident response lifecycle. Students simulated real-world security incidents, developed automated detection and containment tools, and practiced proper incident documentation. These skills are essential for security operations center (SOC) analysts and incident responders. Continue practicing by simulating different attack scenarios and refining your automation scripts.

Key Takeaways:

Incident response follows a structured lifecycle: Detection → Containment → Eradication → Recovery
Automation accelerates response time and ensures consistency
Proper documentation is critical for post-incident analysis
System snapshots preserve forensic evidence
Verification after recovery ensures complete remediation
